And so agentic experience is actually much easier to measure,

736
00:35:25.360 --> 00:35:28.560
because we can spin up an agent's in a box and see whether it does

737
00:35:28.560 --> 00:35:29.800
the thing that we'd expect it

738
00:35:29.800 --> 00:35:32.120
when given a task of shape that we would like,

739
00:35:32.120 --> 00:35:34.760
that we see our customers using in production.

740
00:35:34.760 --> 00:35:37.560
And so that kind of evaluation,

741
00:35:37.560 --> 00:35:41.720
because we can go have a bunch of agents do, it becomes much more tractable.

742
00:35:42.400 --> 00:35:45.440
And so that I think is much more measurable.

743
00:35:45.520 --> 00:35:46.920
However, there is a layer

744
00:35:46.920 --> 00:35:49.960
where we still want humans to enjoy interacting with product.

745
00:35:49.960 --> 00:35:52.080
It can't just be purely optimized for agents.

746
00:35:52.080 --> 00:35:55.880
And also humans do need to interact with tessellations or with other parts

747
00:35:55.880 --> 00:35:57.480
of our product surface.

748
00:35:57.480 --> 00:36:01.280
And I think there we lean much more on kind of qualitative

749
00:36:01.280 --> 00:36:06.800
rather than quantitative measures in terms of listening to what people are saying,

750
00:36:07.360 --> 00:36:11.560
rather than trying to jump straight into kind of quantifying it.

751
00:36:12.080 --> 00:36:16.240
Over time, I imagine that's just partially where we are, the stage of company

752
00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:19.280
that we're at in terms of we have a direct relationship

753
00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:22.000
with the majority of people who are using a product,

754
00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:23.320
particularly in the enterprise setting.

755
00:36:23.320 --> 00:36:27.120
And so we can just go listen, and then by proxy,

756
00:36:27.160 --> 00:36:28.840
like for our internal factory,

757
00:36:28.840 --> 00:36:31.040
all our customers are sitting over there right next to us.

758
00:36:31.040 --> 00:36:32.040
And so they will very happily

759
00:36:32.040 --> 00:36:35.040
come tell us when something's bad or not feeling good.

760
00:36:35.280 --> 00:36:37.480
So I think that's the way that we've been solving it so far.

761
00:36:39.240 --> 00:36:41.720
So thank you so much. Rob.

762
00:36:41.720 --> 00:36:42.960
I'm going to click over.
